{"id":"831207a20d267da0540c75947398b895a554a190","axis":"silent","repo":"bokeh/bokeh","sha":"831207a20d267da0540c75947398b895a554a190","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/bokeh-ci-full.yml","lines":["@@ -262,6 +262,9 @@ jobs:","           run: |","             pyright --version","             pyright","+        - name: Check type completeness of public API with pyright","+          run: |","+            pixi run --locked --environment ${{ matrix.environment }} verify-types"," ","   examples:","     needs: build"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/bokeh-ci.yml","lines":["@@ -231,6 +231,9 @@ jobs:","         - name: Check library types with pyright","           run: |","             pyright --version && pyright","+        - name: Check type completeness of public API with pyright","+          run: |","+            pixi run --locked --environment ${{ matrix.environment }} verify-types"," ","   examples:","     needs: [changes, build]"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/bokeh/source/docs/dev_guide/python.rst","lines":["@@ -196,8 +196,10 @@ Bokeh uses two systems for type checking Python code:","   <https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0484/>`_ style hints. Use the Python","   standard `typing` and `typing_extensions` modules if necessary."," ","-:ref:`Bokeh's CI <contributor_guide_testing_ci>` uses `mypy`_ to check types.","-To type check your code locally, run ``mypy bokeh``.","+:ref:`Bokeh's CI <contributor_guide_testing_ci>` uses `mypy`_ and `pyright`_ to","+check types, and ``pyright --verifytypes`` to guard the type completeness of","+Bokeh's public API. See :ref:`contributor_guide_testing_local_typing` for how to","+run these checks locally."," "," .. note::","     In case you want to use type information with tools other than mypy (such as","@@ -210,5 +212,6 @@ To type check your code locally, run ``mypy bokeh``."," .. _Google Python Style Guide: https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#383-functions-and-methods"," .. _Ruff: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff"," .. _mypy: https://mypy.readthedocs.io","+.. _pyright: https://microsoft.github.io/pyright"," .. _stub files: https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0484/#stub-files"," .. _PEP 604: https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0604/"],"additions":5,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/bokeh/source/docs/dev_guide/testing.rst","lines":["@@ -41,7 +41,8 @@ Whenever you change anything in Bokeh's codebase"," "," When you edit Bokeh's Python code","     Run Bokeh's :ref:`Python unit tests","-    <contributor_guide_testing_local_python_unit>`","+    <contributor_guide_testing_local_python_unit>` and","+    :ref:`type checks <contributor_guide_testing_local_typing>`"," "," When your work involves UI elements","     Run Bokeh's :ref:`Python integration tests","@@ -127,6 +128,43 @@ directory. Changes to these tools should pass their dedicated test suite."," ","     pytest tests/tools"," ","+.. _contributor_guide_testing_local_typing:","+","+Run type checks","+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~","+","+Bokeh's Python code is type checked with both `mypy`_ and `pyright`_. Any edits","+you make to Bokeh's Python code should pass both type checkers.","+","+In addition, the type completeness of Bokeh's public API is measured with","+``pyright --verifytypes``. Type completeness is the share of symbols exported","+by Bokeh (functions, classes, methods, attributes, etc.) whose types are fully","+known, i.e. declared with type annotations or unambiguously inferable, rather","+than unknown or dependent on how a particular type checker infers them. Symbols","+with incomplete types silently degrade type checking to dynamic typing in code","+that uses Bokeh, and may be interpreted differently by different type checkers.","+This check fails when the completeness score drops or the number of exported","+symbols with unknown types increases compared to the baseline recorded in","+:bokeh-tree:`tools/ci/verify_types.py`. When your changes","+improve type completeness, raise the baseline in that file accordingly. To see","+which symbols are incomplete, run ``pyright --verifytypes bokeh --ignoreexternal``.","+","+**Standard terminal:**","+","+.. code-block:: sh","+","+    pixi run mypy","+    pixi run pyright","+    pixi run verify-types","+","+**Inside a pixi shell:**","+","+.. code-block:: sh","+","+    mypy","+    pyright","+    python tools/ci/verify_types.py","+"," .. _contributor_guide_testing_local_python:"," "," Run Python tests","@@ -913,6 +951,8 @@ instead of pushing every commit individually. This will help you be considerate"," of others who require access to these limited resources."," "," .. _Ruff: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff","+.. _mypy: https://mypy.readthedocs.io","+.. _pyright: https://microsoft.github.io/pyright"," .. _pytest: https://pytest.org/"," .. _pytest-xdist: https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest-xdist"," .. _Chromium: https://www.chromium.org/Home"],"additions":41,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pixi.toml","lines":["@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@ test-codebase = \"pytest tests/codebase\""," test-examples = { cmd = \"pytest tests/test_examples.py\", depends-on = [\"install-browser\"] }"," test-tools = \"pytest tests/tools\""," test-docs = \"pytest tests/docs\"","+verify-types = \"python tools/ci/verify_types.py\""," test = \"pytest\""," build-docs = \"bash tools/ci/build_docs.sh\""," install-browser = \"python -m playwright install --only-shell chromium\""],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/bokeh/client/websocket.py","lines":["@@ -47,6 +47,8 @@"," class WebSocketClientConnectionWrapper:","     ''' Used for compatibility across Tornado versions and to add write_lock'''"," ","+    write_lock: locks.Lock","+","     def __init__(self, socket: WebSocketClientConnection) -> None:","         self._socket = socket","         # write_lock allows us to lock the connection to send multiple"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/b